[{"category":"religion_groups","key":"christian","name":"Christianity","description":"Christianity, a prominent Abrahamic faith, centers on the life and teachings of Jesus Christ, emphasizing salvation through faith and adherence to biblical principles. Its diverse branches, including Catholicism, Protestantism, and Eastern Orthodoxy, wield significant influence across the globe, shaping history, politics, and culture.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_catholic","allow_slaves_of_same_group":false,"convert_slaves_at_start":false,"clergy_goods_demand_modifier":{"wine":10}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"buddhist","name":"Buddhism","description":"Having its origins from the teachings of the Buddha, meaning 'The Awakened One' and also known by his princely name Siddhārtha Gautama or by the title #italic Śākyamuni#!, $buddhist$ expanded far and wide from its source in $india$. Influencing and getting influenced by the many countries and peoples and beliefs it spread to, many different $buddhist_ADJ$ schools emerged within it, with different approaches and interpretations on the path to liberation from Saṃsāra, the cycle of death and rebirth.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_group_buddhist","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"muslim","name":"Islam","description":"Islam, a monotheistic religion founded by Prophet Muḥammad in the 7th century, espouses the belief in one God (Allāh) and follows the teachings of the $common_string_quran$. With its various denominations like Sunni and Shia, Islam has profoundly impacted societies, fostering cultural, scientific, and political advancements across continents.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_sunni","allow_slaves_of_same_group":false,"convert_slaves_at_start":true,"modifier":{"allow_rgo_slave_demand":true},"goods_demand_modifier":{"wine":0,"beer":0,"liquor":0}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"dharmic","name":"Dharma","description":"$dharmic_ADJ$ religions have their origin in $india$ and all have in common the concept of 'Dharma', meaning the correct behavior and way of living according to the cosmic laws of the universe.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"color_hindu","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"zoroastrian_group","name":"Zoroastrianism","description":"$zoroastrian_group$ is a grouping of religions that follow the faith created by Zoroaster.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_zoroastrian","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"manichaean_group","name":"Manichaeism","description":"$manichean_group$ refers to those faiths related to the life philosophies that emerged from the teachings of the prophet Mani.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_manichaeism","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"mandean_group","name":"Mandaean","description":"The $mandean_group$ faith groups the ethnoreligious communities that follow this gnostic monotheistic religion.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_mandeaism","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"druze_group","name":"Druze","description":"The $druze_group$ group covers all the religions that fall under this umbrella.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_druzism","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"yazidi_group","name":"Yazidi","description":"The $yazidi_group$ faiths are those beliefs of the ethnoreligious group known as $yazidism_ADJ$.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"religion_yazidism","convert_slaves_at_start":false},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"israelite_group","name":"Israelite","description":"The Jews, descendants of ancient Hebrews, have spread across the known world after the destruction of their homeland. Bound by faith and tradition, they contribute as merchants, scholars, and craftsmen, while maintaining a connection to their shared heritage. Dispersed yet united, they embody a resilient identity, keeping the eternal hope for Zion alive in their hearts.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"map_ISR","allow_slaves_of_same_group":false,"clergy_goods_demand_modifier":{"wine":10}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"folk_african_group","name":"African Folk Religions","description":"The $folk_african_group$ $common_folk_religion_group_desc$ $africa$.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"map_bantu","convert_slaves_at_start":true,"modifier":{"allow_rgo_slave_demand":true}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"folk_argentinian_group","name":"Argentinian Folk Religions","description":"The $folk_argentinian_group$ $common_folk_religion_group_desc$ $name_argentina$.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"map_selknam","convert_slaves_at_start":true,"modifier":{"allow_rgo_slave_demand":true}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"folk_aridoamerica_group","name":"Aridoamerican Folk Religions","description":"The $folk_aridoamerica_group$ $common_folk_religion_group_desc$ $aridoamerica_region$.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"map_selknam","convert_slaves_at_start":true,"modifier":{"allow_rgo_slave_demand":true}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"folk_asian_group","name":"Asian Folk Religions","description":"The $folk_asian_group$ $common_folk_religion_group_desc$ $asia$.","source":{"kind":"base"},"fields":{"color":"map_muong","convert_slaves_at_start":true,"modifier":{"allow_rgo_slave_demand":true}},"crossRefs":[]},{"category":"religion_groups","key":"folk_australian_group","name":"Australian Folk Religions","description":"The $folk_australian_group$ $common_folk_religion_group_desc$ $australia_region$.","sour